        "title": "00-OVERVIEW - Natural Sciences: Field Taxonomy and Unifying Principles",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Everything in natural science is an inquiry at a particular scale.\nUnderstanding *which scale* determines which tools, approximations, and languages apply."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#005",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:natural-sciences:00-overview, git-history:natural-sciences:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "natural-sciences/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "natural-sciences/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:natural-sciences:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "natural-sciences",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "natural-sciences",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "00-OVERVIEW - Natural Sciences: Field Taxonomy and Unifying Principles",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nSCALE        SIZE            FIELD            GOVERNING FRAMEWORK\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nCosmological  >1 Mpc          Cosmology        GR + ΛCDM\nStellar        ~R☉            Astrophysics     plasma physics, nuclear\nPlanetary      ~R♁            Geophysics       continuum mechanics, MHD\n                               Atmosphere       fluid dynamics, radiation\nMacroscopic    cm–km           Classical mech.  Newtonian / thermo\nMesoscopic     µm–mm           Soft matter      stat mech, hydrodynamics\nCellular       1–100 µm        Cell biology     diffusion, reaction–diff.\nMolecular      0.1–10 nm       Chemistry        QM + stat mech\nAtomic         ~0.1 nm         Atomic physics   quantum mechanics (QM)\nNuclear        ~1 fm           Nuclear physics  QCD / nuclear force\nSubatomic      <1 fm           Particle physics QFT / Standard Model\n```"
    },
